# NanoMQ broker demo options
#
# An application-level Kconfig file replaces the top of the Zephyr tree
# (kconfig.cmake: KCONFIG_ROOT = <app>/Kconfig when it exists), so the
# whole Zephyr tree must be pulled back in explicitly.  See
# samples/basic/minimal/Kconfig for the same pattern.

config BROKER_LOG_DEBUG
	bool "Set NanoMQ log level to DEBUG"
	help
	  Bumps nanolib log level from the default WARN to DEBUG so the
	  MQTT session flow is visible on the console.  Disable for normal
	  runs (less noise, fewer cycles in log formatting).

config BROKER_REST_API
	bool "Enable the NanoMQ REST API (HTTP tcp:8081, auth off)"
	help
	  Sets conf http_server.enable / auth_type=NONE_AUTH in main.c so the
	  broker serves /api/v4 over plain HTTP.  Requires an extra SLIRP
	  hostfwd for tcp:8081 (see prj.conf) to be reachable from the host.

config BROKER_WEBHOOK
	bool "Enable the NanoMQ webhook forwarder (POST to conf->web_hook.url)"
	help
	  Sets conf web_hook.enable, an inproc hook channel (Zephyr has no IPC
	  transport) and one MESSAGE_PUBLISH rule on "test/#" so published
	  messages are POSTed to the receiver URL (guest reaches the QEMU host
	  alias 10.0.2.2).  Run a receiver on that port before exercising it.

config BROKER_WS
	bool "Enable the WebSocket listener (MQTT over RFC6455, tcp:8083)"
	help
	  Sets conf websocket.enable / websocket.url in main.c so the broker
	  also accepts MQTT over WebSocket on nmq-ws://0.0.0.0:8083/mqtt.
	  Requires the mqttws transport in the NanoNNG build (enabled by this
	  app's CMakeLists via NNG_TRANSPORT_MQTT_BROKER_WS=ON) and an extra
	  SLIRP hostfwd for tcp:8083 (see prj.conf) to be reachable from the
	  host.  TLS is built out of the Zephyr NanoNNG, so WSS stays inert.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
